    "notes": "Four sessions, 1967: RCA Victor's Studio A, New York City on August 28 (Boo-Dah; Blood Count; U.M.M.G.), August 30 (Raincheck; Rock Skippin' at the Blue Note; Lotus Blossom) and September 1 (Snibor; After All; All Day Long); and San Francisco on November 15 (Charpoy; The Intimacy of the Blues; Day Dream) — the San Francisco date uses Jeff Castleman (bass) and Steve Little (drums) instead of Aaron Bell and Sam Woodyard (S2). Recorded 1967, released 1968 (RCA Victor LSP-3906). Producer Brad McCuen and engineer Ed Begley per Discogs (S2); Wikipedia's infobox also credits Steve Backer as producer (S1) — both preserved. All compositions by Billy Strayhorn except 'Day Dream' (Strayhorn-Ellington) and 'Acht O'Clock Rock' (Ellington, CD bonus track only). The 2016 CD reissue adds seven bonus tracks (Acht O'Clock Rock; Raincheck take 4; Smada takes 3 and 4; Midriff; My Little Brown Book; Lotus Blossom trio version), excluded here as reissue-only (S2). Durations and side layout from the original LP listing (S1); the reissue's timings differ slightly."
  },
  "ballot": {
    "album": "Duke Ellington — ...And His Mother Called Him Bill (1968)",
    "scope_check": {
